{"name":"September Sun","hex":"#fdd7a2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"September Sun","blocks":[{"text":"\"September Sun\" is a single by gothic metal band Type O Negative from the 2007 album Dead Again. The nearly ten minute song was edited to just 4½ minutes for the single release. The single was released on January 14, 2008, ten months after the album's release on March 13, 2007. \"September Sun\" was the band's final single released before the passing of frontman Peter Steele."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_Sun","wikidata":"Q3955677"},{"title":"September","blocks":[{"text":"September is the ninth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg/330px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September","wikidata":"Q123"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_conte